+<span style="font-weight: bold;"> SECTION 40-57-730.</span> Licensure after revocation.<br /><br />
+	(A) Unless the revocation is expressly made permanent as provided for in Section 40-1-120, after revocation of a license, a person may not reapply for three years from the date of revocation.<br /><br />
+	(B) An individual seeking licensure after revocation shall:<br /><br />
+	(1) appear before the commission in order for the commission to evaluate the individual&#39;s competency and fitness to transact the business of a real estate licensee; and<br /><br />
+	(2) meet all applicable educational examination and experience requirements that apply to individuals applying for a license who have never been licensed.<br /><br />
